+# Release candidate preparation evidence
+
+## Source and scope
+
+The release plan fixes stable version 0.7.8, previous tag v0.7.7, and base commit `262da3130bc5628a7641c400c74368ae355000bf`. The copied `release-plan-version.json` and `release-plan-changes.json` preserve the native planner inputs. Release notes contain each of the 1,417 planned commit links exactly once and start with two accessible prose paragraphs.
+
+The candidate updates existing semantic version surfaces, generated references, release notes, release images, and qualification artifacts. Test support shares duplicated fixture planning, release options, and expected run-control output. Route and recovery fixtures now establish the current canonical planning, verification, creation-identity, and replay contracts. The qualification audit also initially identified four bounded runtime defects: missing task-read tracing, dependency waits bypassed by the approved Task projection, unstarted planning-base recovery rejected by that projection, and unusable package dependency links in a fresh worktree. The candidate repairs these paths while preserving recovery tokens, provenance, execution checks, external-root install ownership, release acceptance, and the dependency lockfile.
+
+## Baseline and focused checks
+
+- `bun run ci:local:full`: passed on the integrated preparation base before candidate metadata edits. Captured log SHA-256: `b55efb2ccaa9d2611eb07fa1d6973110671a6adfe2d04d9606ebe8fb0ca8d555`.
+- `bun run framework:dev:bootstrap`: passed for the 0.7.8 candidate checkout.
+- `bun run release:parity`: passed with CLI, core, recipes, internal pins, and recipes runtime at 0.7.8.
+- `bun run docs:site:generate:check`: passed; package reference and full LLM document are fresh.
+- `node scripts/check-release-notes.mjs --tag v0.7.8 --min-bullets 1417`: passed.
+- Prettier checks and `git diff --check`: passed for changed product artifacts.
+
+## Preliminary installed upgrade qualification
+
+`node docs/releases/v0.7.8-evidence/qualify-upgrade-0.7.7.mjs` passed before the implementation commit. This is preparation evidence; the native supervisor reruns the declared command against the committed candidate for formal verification. The script uses a published npm 0.7.7 installation and three locally packed 0.7.8 packages in isolated temporary prefixes. It removes those prefixes and fixture repositories after the run.
+
+| Fixture   | Task before and after            | Upgrade commit                             | Checks                                                                       | Repeat apply                            |
+| --------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
+| direct    | DOING, same identity and content | `1d587c2b2f91c2bca194455ae0d00dfb709e4c66` | doctor, routing, agents, project sentinel, task brief and next action passed | no additional commit or tracked changes |
+| branch_pr | DOING, same identity and content | `68be6a1781791f56b77cf4bf359594d68b485300` | doctor, routing, agents, project sentinel, task brief and next action passed | no additional commit or tracked changes |
+
+The direct fixture retains one worktree. The branch_pr fixture retains its base plus the original active task worktree. Both installed runtimes resolve CLI and core version 0.7.8 outside the framework checkout. Upgrade review reports were read for both fixtures.
+
+## Remaining formal evidence
+
+The native prepublish run on `91b1096d1e098660107b11b97f603baf032c7547` passed the complete `ci:contract` stage, including lint, architecture, clone, unused-code, and coverage-threshold checks. Clone totals are 91 clones, 1,428 duplicated lines, and 9,989 duplicated tokens, within the unchanged baseline. The next stage failed while writing its temporary source archive because the local disk was full. After removing inactive generated test fixtures, `node scripts/check-agentplane-artifacts.mjs` passed on that same commit. This check confirms recovery of the archive step; the complete prepublish result remains pending.
+
+The native gate subsequently reached release CI. Groups 1-8 passed, and group 9 stopped on the readiness fixture. A supplemental audit executed groups 10-113 with the canonical isolation and limits: 5,309 tests passed, 85 failed, and one existing test was skipped. Including the readiness case, 86 failures across 25 CLI test files reproduced on unchanged main. The audit identifies repair scope and does not replace formal native qualification. The repaired fixtures use current verification preconditions, registered task worktrees, canonical batch metadata, and current help snapshots. Runtime corrections are covered by the existing CLI scenarios plus the package install-layout regression. The combined repaired CLI and runtime regression run passed all 193 tests in 28 files. Architecture layering, focused ESLint and formatting, root and testkit TypeScript checks, and the unchanged clone baseline also passed. These focused results precede the committed native rerun.
+
+The subsequent native run on `a5425459b7d369c4987a798241017d4210e60058` passed `ci:contract`, package checks, and release CI groups 1-34. The protected-base fixture then attempted duplicate worktree registration. Its corrected eight-test suite passes. A supplemental audit of groups 36-113 passed 4,918 tests and found 39 missing-export failures in three finish unit-suite mocks, with one existing skip. After completing those mocks, all 52 tests across the four affected suites passed. Both downstream coverage suites passed. The release-critical smoke failure reproduced on unchanged main and passed after adding the required Verify Steps. Packed lifecycle qualification and published 0.7.7 upgrades passed on committed source; an earlier attempt correctly refused the uncommitted test draft. The existing size and clone baselines remain unchanged. The outer native prepublish deadline is now one hour because measured sequential execution exceeds 30 minutes before its downstream stages; individual test and group limits remain unchanged.
+
+The native run on `72494f26912167513f011d365e061f7eda557431` passed `ci:contract`, package checks, and release CI groups 1-54. Group 55 exposed a concurrent initialization race: the exclusive repository identity destination became visible before JSON writing finished. Stack diagnostics and a controlled overlapping-write regression reproduced the empty read. The corrected writer publishes a complete private candidate without replacing the winner. All four authority identity tests pass, including read-only and foreign-base validation, and focused lint, formatting, root types, size and clone guards pass. The unchanged full group 55 rerun passes all 120 tests in ten files after rebuilding the CLI. Final native committed qualification remains pending.
+
+The preparation WorkItem completed all four native checks on `1c6243bee363042ed51fff599a17a34f83aa2ae2`: prepublish passed in 39 minutes, packed lifecycle passed, published 0.7.7 upgrade passed, and release notes passed. The later Task-level run on `abca029ba` passed every release test group but failed because the branch verification driver omitted the approved command metadata and applied its default 30-minute deadline. The parent process received SIGTERM; passing test output does not make that verification successful. A separate internal WorkItem preserves the completed preparation evidence and forwards the Task plan through the existing verification primitives. The regression fails on the old implementation and passes after correction. Both related suites pass all 47 tests, including legacy fallback and the frozen verification snapshot. Focused lint, formatting, root types, and unchanged size and clone guards pass. Native Task-level qualification remains pending with the original four commands and approved deadlines.
+
+The declared native checks include canonical prepublish, packed mixed-scope lifecycle, the exact published upgrade script, and release-note validation. Their results must be attached to the committed implementation by AgentPlane. Publication is still pending at this preparation stage and requires integrated main, exact-SHA hosted release-ready evidence, explicit GitHub workflow dispatch, canonical publish-result, and public distribution readback.
